Lock screen: stop fingerprint retries once the session is unlocked

After a failed or cancelled fingerprint attempt, the lock screen retries
(retryOnFail, and an error-retry timer) without checking that it is still
locked. Unlocking with the password left those retries running, holding
the fingerprint reader, so sudo and polkit got "Device was already
claimed" and fell back to the password. Found on an HP EliteBook 8 G1i.

--- a/modules/lock/Pam.qml
+++ b/modules/lock/Pam.qml
@@ -230,7 +230,9 @@
             configDirectory: Quickshell.shellPath("assets/pam.d")
 
             onCompleted: res => {
-                if (!ctx.available)
+                // Once unlocked, stop: retrying would keep claiming the
+                // fingerprint reader, and sudo and polkit couldn't use it.
+                if (!ctx.available || !root.lock.secure)
                     return;
 
                 if (res === PamResult.Success)
@@ -266,7 +268,10 @@
             id: errorRetry
 
             interval: 800
-            onTriggered: pam.start()
+            onTriggered: {
+                if (ctx.canAttempt)
+                    pam.start();
+            }
         }
 
         Timer {
